; A ScrollContainer whose own size is FRACTIONAL, so each scrollbar's own rect
; origin lands on a half pixel.
;
; The one variable: whether a ScrollContainer's scrollbars are snapped to whole
; pixels at their OWN draw origin. Godot's `h_scroll`/`v_scroll` are real
; HScrollBar/VScrollBar Control nodes added as INTERNAL_MODE_BACK children, so
; each is its own CanvasItem and `Control::_update_canvas_item_transform` floors
; each one's translation INDEPENDENTLY of the container's. Chrome drawn inside
; the container's own group inherits only the container's snap and never gets
; its own.
;
; `Scroll` is 900.5 x 600.5 at the integer origin (100, 20). Its position is
; already whole, so the container's own snap is a no-op and cannot mask the
; bars': everything that moves here moves because a BAR was or was not snapped.
; The bar thickness is a whole 8 px at every theme scale (`2 * content_margin`),
; so the horizontal bar's own top is 600.5 - 8 = 592.5 and the vertical bar's
; own left is 900.5 - 8 = 892.5 — both exactly half a pixel off, the largest
; error the snap can produce. Snapped they are 593 and 893, i.e. absolute
; y = 613 and x = 993.
;
; `Canvas` is a single flat 1200 x 900 fill, larger than the viewport in both
; axes so both bars are visible, and BRIGHT so each bar's outer edge is the
; biggest channel step this scene can offer: the default theme leaves
; ScrollContainer's own panel empty and the track and grabber styleboxes are
; near-black AND 60% transparent, so over anything dark a half-pixel edge blend
; is a couple of levels and reads as noise.
;
; That edge is what the picture is. StyleBoxFlat's anti-aliasing feathers an
; edge over one pixel centred on it, so an edge on a pixel BOUNDARY leaves both
; neighbouring pixel centres at full coverage or none, while an edge on a pixel
; CENTRE puts that centre at exactly half. Snapped, the row above the horizontal
; bar (y = 612) is pure fill and the row below (y = 613) is pure track;
; unsnapped, y = 612 is a 50/50 blend of the two. Same for x = 992 / 993 at the
; vertical bar. Nothing else in the goldens has a Control whose own chrome is
; drawn by a nested CanvasItem, and the other ScrollContainer scene is 600 x 500
; — whole numbers, whose bar origins are (0, 492) and (592, 0) — so an
; unsnapped bar is invisible in every other baseline.
;
; Measured against Godot 4.6.3 at `--mode 2d`. The fill reads rgb(242, 230, 64)
; and the track over it rgb(113, 108, 42). Horizontal bar, x = 900:
; y = 610/611/612 are all rgb(242, 230, 64) and y = 613/614/615 all
; rgb(113, 108, 42). Vertical bar, y = 550: x = 990/991/992 are all
; rgb(242, 230, 64) and x = 993/994/995 all rgb(113, 108, 42). No blended pixel
; at either boundary — only possible if each bar snapped its own origin.
;
; The same render proves the feather is live rather than absent, so those crisp
; edges cannot be an un-antialiased rasteriser resolving a tie: the horizontal
; grabber's own right edge is a genuinely fractional 765.8, and at y = 616 it
; reads rgb(170, 167, 127) at x = 763/764, rgb(158, 154, 109) at x = 765 and
; rgb(113, 108, 42) at x = 766 — the 0.8 coverage a one-pixel feather predicts
; (0.8 * 170 + 0.2 * 113 = 158.6). A grabber offset is drawn INSIDE the bar's
; own CanvasItem and so is never snapped; only the bar's own origin is.
;
; Snapping pushes each bar's FAR edge INTO the container's clip, which sits on a
; fraction — the horizontal bar now ends at absolute y = 621 against a clip at
; 620.5, the vertical one at x = 1001 against 1000.5 — so the scene measures
; that side too. Godot cuts it whole-pixel, not proportionally: at x = 900,
; y = 618/619/620 are all rgb(113, 108, 42) and y = 621/622 are the backdrop
; rgb(20, 23, 31); at y = 550, x = 998/999/1000 are all rgb(113, 108, 42) and
; x = 1001/1002 the backdrop. No partial row or column at either boundary.
;
; The snap also opens a half-pixel SEAM in the corner where the bars meet, which
; nothing else in the goldens has: the horizontal bar's own right edge is
; `rect.w - thickness` = 992.5 and stays fractional (it is a size, and sizes are
; never snapped), while the vertical bar's left edge is the snapped 993. At
; y = 616 Godot reads rgb(113, 108, 42) at x = 991, rgb(186, 177, 54) at
; x = 992 and the untouched fill rgb(242, 230, 64) at x = 993/994.

[gd_scene format=3]

[node name="Root" type="Control"]
anchors_preset = 15
anchor_right = 1.0
anchor_bottom = 1.0

[node name="Backdrop" type="ColorRect" parent="."]
anchors_preset = 15
anchor_right = 1.0
anchor_bottom = 1.0
color = Color(0.08, 0.09, 0.12, 1)

[node name="Scroll" type="ScrollContainer" parent="."]
anchors_preset = 0
offset_left = 100.0
offset_top = 20.0
offset_right = 1000.5
offset_bottom = 620.5

[node name="Canvas" type="ColorRect" parent="Scroll"]
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(1200, 900)
layout_mode = 2
color = Color(0.95, 0.9, 0.25, 1)
